Z||000000||Richard Parnell||01-18-2000||02:41 PM||||I love my Fiero and am in the slow process of building and restoring it to the condition I like.  I look at it this way, even if I put $10K into the car (which I bought for $1K) I will have a car that is better than a new car, a car that is fairly unique and it will be faster and better looking than anything I could buy new for $20+K.  Plus I know everything about the car.||||reg||6
Z||000001||1FST2M6||01-18-2000||02:54 PM||||HERE HERE! I've sunk a pretty penny into my car and can always say "its paid for" and oh what was that "I just SMOKED your new Mustang GT... awww thats too bad... hahaha " and laugh all the way to the bank! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||01-18-2000||03:30 PM||||Richard,<P>In addition to all that you said, you will have a unique car (soon to be classic), and in my case (since I do all my own work), I can say "I rebuilt it from the ground up."<P>I like having the confidence of knowing that I have a reliable ride.  On Xmas eve I saw two 2000 model Corvettes on the side of the road with flashers on.  New, is no guarantee for reliable.||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||01-18-2000||03:50 PM||||mshill,<P>I usually stop and offer rides to broken down folks and I would say that 90% are out of gas.  Most of the other 10% have lost a tire.  I find it extremely hard to believe that the LS-1 has stranded many passengers and for that matter that many new vehicles have done so.  <P>Everyone,<P>Now on the topic.  I am in the process of doing the same to my car.  I have a budget in the 7 G range for my "new" Fiero and am going to do as much as possible by myself.  I want my project to not only be fast but beautiful and near show worthy when complete.  For the most part, new cars simply do not excite me.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000004||Monkeyman||01-18-2000||04:51 PM||||Ditto, William.  I haven't set a budget for my '85 GT (another $300 and it's mine!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), but I plan on doing all of the work myself with the exception of the brakes and steering.  If I screw something else up, I may end up on the side of the road and embarrassed, but probably not dead.  I tend to mess things up pretty well.||||reg||1
Z||000005||SpeedPhreak||01-18-2000||05:41 PM||||u know i never really thought of it that way.  my main reason for buying a fiero was to build a kit.  i figured i would be replacing all the suspension & drivetrain, interior, exterior, etc...  so i guess i was thinking along the lines.<P>n e way, i know its not ponty or gm for that matter but has anyone seen that mopar is bringing back the HEMI  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> & not just as a block & parts you order to build yourself (i know thats been around for awhile).  they have it in the magazines in the new 300m, it sure is perty.  they are talking about putting it in the new charger (oh my god i gotta get 1 or 2...yea like i could afford 1) & they are trying to get the nascar ban lifted so they can race it in super trucks.<P>i love mopar & this is great news to me, like most people here new cars dont excite me much but these do!<BR>||||reg||1
